<speak>I spread them across the dining table, which is why I am enjoying the clear table today. For a while nobody could eat there without moving a pile. My husband was very patient, although he kept asking whether a particular pile was finished. I had a pile for things to keep, one for things to look at again, and one for items that were not even mine. The middle pile was the problem. It kept growing because postponing a decision was so easy.</speak>